Description: Red Pitaya app stack for Web-888 (RX-888) SDR - Debian build
 From-source build of the RaspSDR/red-pitaya-notes SDR applications
 (vendor fork of pavel-demin/red-pitaya-notes, MIT license), with
 vendored factory FPGA bitstreams, fully systemd-managed and disabled
 by default: WebSDR stays the default-on service, RP apps are opt-in.
 .
 Ships web888-rpapp@.service template units (bitstream load in
 ExecStartPre, Conflicts=web888-websdr.service both directions) and
 /usr/sbin/web888-mode for runtime switching between WebSDR mode and
 any RP app. v1 apps: sdr_receiver_hpsdr (Thetis/cuSDR/SparkSDR
 clients), sdr_receiver (raw I/Q TCP), sdr_transceiver_wide (GNU Radio
 gr-osmosdr), led_blinker (FPGA-load smoke test).

